  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>m</mi></math> is the minimum value of <math><mi>k</mi></math> for which the function <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi></math> is increasing in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mn>0,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo></math> and <math><mi>M</mi></math> is the maximum value of <math><mi>f</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mn>0,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo></math> when <math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the ordered pair <math><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to:"
  },
